angular-signal-input-transform-undefined:
When migrating @Input() properties with default values in Servoy components to signal inputs:

PROBLEM: In Servoy, form templates bind ALL model properties: `[pane1MinSize]="model.pane1MinSize"`. If the server never sends a value, `model.pane1MinSize` is `undefined`. Angular evaluates the binding and passes `undefined` to the input, overriding any default value set via `input<any>(30)`. The default only applies if the input is NEVER BOUND in the template.

SOLUTION: Use input transform to coalesce undefined back to the default:
```typescript
readonly pane1MinSize = input(30, { transform: (v: any) => v ?? 30 });
```

OLD PATTERN (pre-signal):
```typescript
@Input() pane1MinSize: any;
svyOnInit() {
  if (this.pane1MinSize == undefined) this.pane1MinSize = 30;
}
```

NEW PATTERN (signal):
```typescript
readonly pane1MinSize = input(30, { transform: (v: any) => v ?? 30 });
// No svyOnInit override needed
```

This applies to ALL Servoy component packages (bootstrapcomponents, bootstrapextracomponents, servoy-extra-components, aggridcomponents) whenever a property has a default value that must survive an undefined push from the server.
